65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341387" :question/id #uuid "fc242beb-e0b4-5693-bd2c-ce902afdb155" :question/math-academy-id "q-341387" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ for $s>4$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[0,\\infty ),$ $f(0)=6,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{6s-10}{{s}^{2}-2s-8},\\,s>4.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{′}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{6s-10}{{s}^{2}-2s-8}-6 \\\\  & =\\frac{s(6s-10)-6({s}^{2}-2s-8)}{{s}^{2}-2s-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{2s+48}{{s}^{2}-2s-8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341387/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51f6b682-ce7e-5068-8679-06a452eed647"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64324/selection/5408f73cc80f263cf70ad8074d91a91196e55ece05b73cb1b4e8d8526b19e506" :answer/id #uuid "a9128768-0024-5e91-a635-41f9d4a98215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s-1}{s-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64324/selection/4153f0e3df98cc64b4b48ab7acb12182582e1e19b3813029b6e241722afaa84a" :answer/id #uuid "b4cb6aae-ed0e-5f32-b282-085fa4d38df0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{s-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64324/selection/fbf279c1135714d8652cf972f4d90856fd3d8d095a2f910d7ff6720eff676221" :answer/id #uuid "b1192b6d-1cd3-52c4-8f7e-1dfebed6d73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id