herefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{5s-4}{{s}^{2}-s}-5 \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{5s-4}{s(s-1)}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5s-4}{s-1}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89453/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51f6b682-ce7e-5068-8679-06a452eed647"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89453"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection/ac2ef4d70505ce76242194ab352ab5f8ee568d16a1bc5537297c83f5ab2e8bbd" :answer/id #uuid "c9745859-3869-586d-8478-50ad98ac24a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s-1}{s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection/c46d04c4de19cb95f52fec4c0e12168978708d0f46cb696f00510e250f846687" :answer/id #uuid "a871c604-07f1-5484-a04a-f29166494d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s+1}{s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection/a91c0036aabcab62d062f84a134e44163114b489dff85543a163a70d636bbbeb" :answer/id #uuid "4f519b89-0737-5021-8f3d-cbd22650371c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection/2ee044a190ac39a890aab9329084d0d2bd396c78a9cf206d2a9dbc13638e1e40" :answer/id #uuid "2d80e3d6-146c-5a3c-8489-a1e677d41a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s-1}{s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection/e55227913973cb367b9301d449c57087e181bfceb81b9bf9e23f2a903b98226c" :answer/id #uuid "010d1c43-b126-5eca-ae33-5418560a95d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db14e2b0-d47e-5c8b-9f7b-9619376c3724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79442/selection/e55227913973cb367b9301d449c57087e181bfceb81b9bf9e23f2a903b98226c" :answer-field/choices ["q-79442/selection/ac2ef4d70505ce76242194ab352ab5f8ee568d16a1bc5537297c83f5ab2e8bbd" "q-79442/selection/c46d04c4de19cb95f52fec4c0e12168978708d0f46cb696f00510e250f846687" "q-79442/selection/a91c0036aabcab62d062f84a134e44163114b489dff85543a163a70d636bbbeb" "q-79442/selection/2ee044a190ac39a890aab9329084d0d2bd396c78a9cf206d2a9dbc13638e1e40" "q-79442/selection/e55227913973cb367b9301d449c57087e181bfceb81b9bf9e23f2a903b98226c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79442" :question/id #uuid "ffd06a54-7e44-5293-ae8a-dc261cf4b9af" :question/math-academy-id "q-79442" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ for $s>2$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[0,\\infty ),$ $f(0)=0,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-2s},\\,s>2.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{′}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-2s}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2s}{s(s-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79442/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51f6b682-ce7e-5068-8679-06a452eed647"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79442"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79443/selection/454dee600bdc4cf537ddd79d3f8f76220de8ab661d50ad69d37177573ce486a4" :answer/id #uuid "6d2e017c-ef16-581d-b627-6e34e16d68a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3s-4}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79443/sel