 ),$ ${f}^{′}(0)=4,$ $f(0)=2,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{2s-4}{{s}^{2}-4s+3},\\,s>3.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{″}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2s-4}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}-s\\cdot 2-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}-2(s+2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{s}^{2}(s-2)-({s}^{2}-4s+3)(s+2)}{{s}^{2}-4s+3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{({s}^{3}-2{s}^{2})-({s}^{3}-2{s}^{2}-5s+6)}{{s}^{2}-4s+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10s-12}{{s}^{2}-4s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79443/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e59d43c-f723-521e-b7cf-6767195483c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79443"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64408/selection/33b49d02a17600dc37fb4397d68b80cac971f51392567c182a01ff403005fb91" :answer/id #uuid "619aa848-4afa-5500-80f4-45b05e4ecbd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3s-1}{{s}^{2}+s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64408/selection/2a09734a366e67287af5e3139582b31633b4a97bae22ec408aed3871c662ce2f" :answer/id #uuid "4026598c-9efd-5ee4-8d49-bf6cc091159a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4s+1}{{s}^{2}+s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64408/selection/94e640f7196207d726958dbce60d4678d5a0fc50d573a8edeb68ed3c7d370eab" :answer/id #uuid "e410348e-6d99-5df1-82c7-882049af1033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s-4}{{s}^{2}+s-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} 